{"pages":[{"w":612.0,"h":792.0,"s":[[13.889,2.206,18.17,3.8,3.431,"EQUINOX"],[13.889,5.306,14.953,1.205,1.078,"Q U A N T I T A T I V E"],[69.444,2.807,15.359,1.643,1.471,"India Equity Research"],[69.444,4.27,11.266,1.46,1.307,"14 November 2026"],[13.889,10.995,11.529,3.651,3.268,"Swiggy"],[13.889,14.731,40.52,2.373,2.124,"Food pays the bills; Instamart sets the price"],[13.889,20.845,52.957,1.809,1.634,"Swiggy has lost 17% since its Q2 FY27 results on 22 October and is 52% below"],[13.889,22.289,52.931,1.809,1.634,"its ₹390 IPO price. Food was not the problem: GOV grew 17.7% and Adjusted"],[13.889,23.733,52.931,1.809,1.634,"EBITDA hit a record ₹341 cr, 3.4% of GOV. Instamart was. After contribution"],[13.889,25.177,52.954,1.809,1.634,"breakeven in May it spent to restart growth: contribution margin fell to −1.0%"],[13.889,26.621,52.987,1.809,1.634,"and the loss rose to ₹895 cr. Toing, a budget-meals app, took Platform"],[13.889,28.065,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Innovations’ loss to ₹162 cr from ₹46 cr a year ago. Blinkit grew NOV 79% to"],[13.889,29.509,45.445,1.809,1.634,"₹20,940 cr, 3.2 times Instamart’s, with Adjusted EBITDA of ₹184 cr."],[13.889,31.995,52.954,1.809,1.634,"1) Food GOV grows 18%, 17% and 16% in FY27-29E; margin reaches 4.3%"],[13.889,33.439,52.931,1.809,1.634,"(guidance: 5%). 2) Instamart NOV grows 36%, 29% and 26%; contribution"],[13.889,34.883,52.987,1.809,1.634,"margin is zero by Q4, 1.8% in FY28E and 3.0% in FY29E, with c.80bp from"],[13.889,36.328,52.934,1.809,1.634,"owning inventory. 3) Costs below contribution, ₹803 cr in Q2, grow 0.4 times as"],[13.889,37.772,52.931,1.809,1.634,"fast as GOV, as they have for five quarters. Adjusted EBITDA turns positive in"],[13.889,39.216,52.934,1.809,1.634,"FY30E; Instamart breaks even in FY31E. Our FY31E Adjusted EBITDA is"],[13.889,40.684,52.931,1.809,1.634,"₹3,629 cr against the ₹10,000 cr target, and EPS ₹9 against ₹30-33. Adjusted"],[13.889,42.128,52.951,1.809,1.634,"EBITDA excludes stock pay: near zero in FY29E, yet the net loss is ₹1,102 cr."],[13.889,43.572,41.585,1.809,1.634,"Cash of ₹13,662 cr troughs at ₹9,040 cr: no new equity needed."],[13.889,46.034,52.931,1.809,1.634,"Our Dec-27 target of ₹210 averages two methods. A 37x P/E, midway between"],[13.889,47.502,52.964,1.809,1.634,"the 52x median of listed Indian internet and consumer names and the 22x of"],[13.889,48.946,52.951,1.809,1.634,"global delivery platforms, on fully-taxed FY31E EPS of ₹6.7, discounted at 12%,"],[13.889,50.39,52.934,1.809,1.634,"plus ₹8 for tax losses, gives ₹200. A DCF to FY36E (5.5% terminal growth) plus"],[13.889,51.834,52.964,1.809,1.634,"cash gives ₹220. Instamart sets the answer: at a long-run margin of 1.5% of"],[13.889,53.278,52.931,1.809,1.634,"GOV the same method gives ₹120, at 4.5% ₹300. We use 3.0%; the price"],[13.889,54.722,52.966,1.809,1.634,"implies 2.6%. The consensus mean target is ₹303. We rate the shares Neutral"],[13.889,56.167,52.931,1.809,1.634,"(ladder: −5% to +15%). Upside: Blinkit-like margins, Toing widening the food"],[13.889,57.611,49.581,1.809,1.634,"market. Downside: e-commerce majors in quick commerce, Rapido in food."],[13.889,60.098,13.042,1.643,1.471,"Price Performance"],[15.268,68.709,1.489,1.022,0.915,"100"],[15.268,66.942,1.489,1.022,0.915,"200"],[15.268,65.174,1.489,1.022,0.915,"300"],[15.268,63.407,1.489,1.022,0.915,"400"],[15.268,61.639,1.489,1.022,0.915,"500"],[18.306,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Jan 26"],[22.929,69.404,2.796,1.022,0.915,"Apr 26"],[27.701,69.404,2.47,1.022,0.915,"Jul 26"],[32.473,69.404,2.96,1.022,0.915,"Oct 26"],[18.53,70.575,3.459,1.275,1.111,"Swiggy ("],[21.992,70.601,0.618,1.241,1.111,"₹"],[22.605,70.575,0.303,1.275,1.111,")"],[25.689,70.575,7.901,1.275,1.111,"NIFTY 50 (rebased)"],[20.285,71.735,1.972,1.387,1.209,"YTD"],[25.556,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"1m"],[30.276,71.735,1.433,1.387,1.209,"3m"],[34.446,71.735,1.984,1.387,1.209,"12m"],[15.277,72.8,1.691,1.387,1.209,"Abs"],[18.784,72.8,3.394,1.387,1.209,"−51.7%"],[23.504,72.8,